The politeness level only checks component-test `errorCount`, but the PR description states the announcement should be `assertive` when 'component test errors **or** accessibility errors are present.' A run with zero component errors but non-zero a11y errors will silently announce as `polite` when it should be `assertive`.

The fix requires hoisting `a11yErrorCount` out of the `if (hasA11yAddon)` block so it is in scope at the `announce` call:

```ts
let a11yErrorCount = 0;
if (hasA11yAddon) {
  a11yErrorCount = a11yStatusValueToStoryIds['status-value:error'].length;
  // ... rest of block unchanged
}

announce(message, errorCount > 0 || a11yErrorCount > 0 ? 'assertive' : 'polite');
```

Note that the `AnnouncesTestRunFinished` story only verifies the `assertive` case for component errors — there is no story covering the a11y-errors-only path, so this bug would go undetected by the current test suite.
